1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:04,610
More on the etiquette of sharʿī ruqyah — what you need as the patient before you begin:

2
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:05,220
First:

3
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:06,350
Think well of Allah,

4
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:07,960
for He is as His servant expects Him to be,

5
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:09,440
and do not rush the result,

6
00:00:09,670 --> 00:00:12,010
for healing comes in the time He wills.

7
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:12,930
Second:

8
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:15,050
Repeat the ruqyah and keep at it,

9
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:17,180
for a servant’s prayer is answered as long as he does not grow hasty.

10
00:00:17,690 --> 00:00:18,050
Third:

11
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:19,590
Seek forgiveness and turn back to Allah,

12
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:22,050
keep up the prayers and the morning and evening adhkar,

13
00:00:22,540 --> 00:00:24,000
for obedience is the lasting fortress.

14
00:00:24,590 --> 00:00:25,010
Fourth:

15
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,060
Be patient with the trial,

16
00:00:26,390 --> 00:00:27,630
for illness expiates sins

17
00:00:27,910 --> 00:00:28,850
and raises ranks

18
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:30,470
when the believer is patient and seeks reward from Allah.

19
00:00:31,070 --> 00:00:31,470
Fifth:

20
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:32,920
Do not become attached to the reciter,

21
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:35,620
and do not make the success of ruqyah depend on one person,

22
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:36,810
for the Healer is Allah.

23
00:00:37,290 --> 00:00:39,130
If the illness drags on or the symptoms worsen,

24
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:42,110
see a doctor while continuing the ruqyah and du‘a.

25
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:45,400
Send this clip to someone you love, and follow the channel.

